for the lower end models once they  get rid of the notch so if you're  somebody that want a touch id in a pro  iphone it likely won't ever happen  another thing that likely won't ever  happen is getting a better port on the  iphones we had rumors of usb type c  coming to iphone pros a while ago and to  make it line up with their other devices  like the macbooks and ipads but nope  apple is still sticking with lightning  all while at the same time changing even  their second cheapest ipad to usb type-c  by this point we can pretty much bet  that usb type-c will never hit iphones  or else apple would have done it by now  but the other rumor also didn't show and  that is the portless iphone 13 at least  on the largest pro max model a  completely wireless iphone was  apparently planned for the highest end  iphone in 2021 and it would make sense  to start out with the pro model but it  looks like apple is holding off which  i'm personally really happy about  because of another thing that  unfortunately didn't come to light with  iphone 13s which i was really looking  for and that is better max save  connectivity and charging not only did  we get rumors of this but actual fcc  filings which reveal a new mac safe unit  now the filing doesn't give us too much  info but apple did test it with both 20  watts and 30 watt adapters as we know if  you're using a 20 watt adapter with the  current max safe puck you will achieve a  max output of 15 watts so about a 75  efficiency so with 30 watts that would  give us 22.5 watts or possibly even up  to 25 wireless fast charging if they  improve the efficiency with the new coil  now that would make it even faster than  using a wire charger and that would be  enough to make a fully wireless iphone  possible but unfortunately nope we are  still stuck with lightning instead of  usb type c and even though the battery  inside of the 13 pro max is 18 larger  than last year's even the wired 20 watt  adapter can no longer charge the phone  to 50 in 30 minutes max of charging  isn't any faster like it was rumored to  be so at this point it will take more  than twice as long to wirelessly fast  charge the 13 pro max then with using a  wire charger with that the first reviews  are coming out and the newer stronger  magsafe magnets are nowhere to be seen  in these new iphone 13s now this is  something that i was really excited for  so that i would have a stronger grip for  my wallet with the 13s and to hold my  phone up better with my magsafe mounts  for my car and my truck and the stronger  magnets would be very helpful because  these new iphones have gotten a lot  heavier than last year the smaller 13  pro with its 6.1 is display now weighs  the same exact as the galaxy note 20  ultra with its 6.9 inch display that  thing is big and the pro max is now  getting closer to the fold 3 meaning  that they will have a harder time  holding on to mounted accessories  thankfully cases could help like this  new slim 13 pro max carbon fiber case  from pitaka which i have been testing  with my 12 pro max that kind of fits and  the slim magnets that are in here are  incredibly strong the strongest i've  ever seen now they're not a sponsor or  anything like that but i'll go ahead and  link them down in the video description  the next missing feature that should  have come out with iphone 13s is the  always on display android phones have  had this feature for years and many have  been expecting this since the iphones  have gotten all its screens which was  the iphone 10 but nope this year was  special though because apple switched to  a more power efficient ltpo screen that  can now go all the way down to 10 hertz  saving a lot of battery life and with  that battery slices have also gotten a  lot larger and the a15 and the new modem  chip are also more power efficient so  this year would have been perfect to add  an always on display but of course they  didn't do that even though apple has  offered this for a few years now with  their apple watches and with the series  7 it gets even brighter indoors they do  not want to add this and this is a  softer feature so they could add it but  apple just doesn't want to my guess is  that's just one more thing they're  adding and keeping for the iphone 14  since this year we got a lot of  incremental updates including that 120  hertz promotion display the next feature  is something that was huge news before  the 13's launch and it was a feature  that would set the iphone apart from any  other smartphone and that is support for  satellite connectivity wow and bloomberg  both reported on this being a feature  that could allow you to connect in  places without cellular connectivity now  i've found myself in this spot many  times and it truly does suck especially  if you have an emergency and this would  allow you to send messages through  satellites when you have no service at  all now some people say this could be a  feature that apple just didn't talk  about because it's not ready yet the  hardware is there but it's not enabled  personally i think if it was there apple  would talk about it and they would say  this is coming in the future because  this would be a killer feature so i  think this is going to have to be  something that's going to come out with  an iphone 14 or later once apple has  their own modems ready with that we have  wi-fi 6e which would have been great  even if it was available for just the  pro models samsung's s21 ultra has  support for it even though it came out  about nine months ago and it allows for  the new six gigahertz band to be used  along with the standard 2.4 and 5  gigahertz bands almost everybody has  wi-fi routers now so there is so much  traffic going around that you can have  interference with each other and  slowdowns and this new band would be  like getting an open freeway while  everybody else is in stop and go traffic  and since most people keep their phones  for years it would've been great to see  it in these new iphones but no and the  same thing goes for bluetooth while the  s21 ultra has bluetooth 5.2 now which  has many improvements iphone is still  stuck on bluetooth 5.0 that uses more  power has more interference issues and  lacks new features one thing we really  wanted to see is an implementation of  lossless audio over wireless since apple  has been really pushing lossless with  apple music and the quality difference  over spotify made me sign up for apple  music again we know it's possible  because qualcomm showed off their  lossless audio over bluetooth with aptx  lossless but of course apple doesn't  support the previous aptx codec either  so they would need to make their own  solution but if they are sticking to  bluetooth 5.0 hardware again and again  there simply isn't the hardware there to  allow this to happen and that means that  the upcoming airpods 3 will not support  lossless either so we will have to wait  now one feature that we know is there  but we are not allowed to use is reverse  wireless charging now i was thinking  apple would finally allow us to use it  outside of the magsafe battery pack  since we have larger batteries this year  but nope not yet  let's hope that with those airpods 3  they will roll out a softer update to  finally let us utilize it because that  can be something that is very handy the  last ones are cameras apple made a huge  deal about them at their event they  spent so much time on the larger sensors  the new lenses the new software but the  selfie camera was completely unchanged  now personally i would love to have a  cut down version of the center stage  cameras that they are putting into most  of their tablets now even the cheapest  basic ipad 9 so something that offers a  wider field of view when you need it and  that can also crop in for selfies and  face time the 12 megapixel camera and  the lens are identical to the iphone 12s  so let's hope that the smart hdr4 will  make a big enough difference to catch  apple up to samsung which has been  killing them lately and selfie quality  now we will know soon enough as soon as  we get our hands on the iphone 13s this  friday and we will put the cameras to  the test in our blind camera comparisons  which are always a ton of fun and they  are completely unbiased so if you guys  want to see that click that circle above  to subscribe and with that you guys can  help us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers we would greatly appreciate  it go ahead and check out one of those  great videos right over there that's  been max and i'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

